WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.740 --> 00:00:02.940
Not every remake has to be bad.

00:00:03.060 --> 00:00:07.880
Some are marked improvements over the original,
others are able to reimagine things just enough

00:00:07.880 --> 00:00:09.740
to stay fresh and interesting.

00:00:10.100 --> 00:00:14.060
Let's take a look at a genre that often does
well with modern updates: horror.

00:00:14.680 --> 00:00:16.280
This is a bit of an odd one.

00:00:16.700 --> 00:00:22.380
Fantasy Island was a TV series that debuted
in the late 1970s and ran for seven seasons.

00:00:22.680 --> 00:00:27.180
It starred Ricardo Montalban as Mr. Roarke,
the caretaker of the titular island where

00:00:27.180 --> 00:00:30.420
guests paid a premium fee to live out their
deepest fantasies.

00:00:30.540 --> 00:00:35.040
The show typically dealt in intrigue, wonder,
and the occasional drama, although some of

00:00:35.040 --> 00:00:38.300
the guests' fantasies took a turn into Twilight
Zone-esque territory.

00:00:38.520 --> 00:00:41.260
Just a little twist, and you've got yourself
a horror movie.

00:00:41.780 --> 00:00:46.440
Blumhouse is bringing Fantasy Island to the
21st century and the big screen, leaning hard

00:00:46.440 --> 00:00:48.720
into the horrific potential of the concept.

00:00:49.080 --> 00:00:54.320
This time, the island is shown twisting people's
wishes beyond their control and creating dangerous,

00:00:54.320 --> 00:00:55.580
horrifying scenarios.

00:00:55.920 --> 00:01:00.750
The movie stars Michael Pena in Montalban's
role, and also features Lucy Hale, Michael

00:01:00.750 --> 00:01:02.580
Rooker, and Parisa Fitz-Henley.

00:01:02.860 --> 00:01:07.320
It's directed by Jeff Wadlow, who directed
Truth or Dare and has produced some successful

00:01:07.320 --> 00:01:08.280
horror television.

00:01:08.460 --> 00:01:12.700
Fantasy Island is an interesting choice for
a horror reboot, as the show always had a

00:01:12.720 --> 00:01:16.580
sinister undercurrent but generally shied
away from outright scares.

00:01:16.780 --> 00:01:21.640
Hopefully making the horrors of granting secret
wishes more overt won't dilute the appeal.

00:01:22.400 --> 00:01:26.340
For being such a product of the '90s, the
original version of The Craft still holds

00:01:26.340 --> 00:01:27.260
up pretty well.

00:01:27.500 --> 00:01:31.500
The story of a group of high school girls
exacting revenge through magical powers is

00:01:31.509 --> 00:01:36.270
a good one, and the central cast of Robin
Tunney, Neve Campbell, Rachel True, and Fairuza

00:01:36.270 --> 00:01:40.480
Balk go through awesome transformations as
the film builds to its conclusion.

00:01:40.640 --> 00:01:43.500
"Aw, relax, it's only magic."

00:01:44.000 --> 00:01:46.180
The reboot of The Craft is coming along nicely.

00:01:46.520 --> 00:01:50.120
Blumhouse has announced that the witches in
their new version will be played by Cailee

00:01:50.139 --> 00:01:53.580
Spaeny, Gideon Adlon, Lovie Simone, and Zoey
Luna.

00:01:53.580 --> 00:01:56.460
The remake is written and directed by Zoe
Lister-Jones.

00:01:56.820 --> 00:02:00.660
One thing that bodes very well for The Craft
reboot is how many people who were involved

00:02:00.660 --> 00:02:03.520
with the original film are also involved with
the update.

00:02:03.780 --> 00:02:08.030
Douglas Wick, who produced the original, is
back as a producer on the reboot, and the

00:02:08.030 --> 00:02:11.800
original film's director, Andrew Fleming,
is also involved in a producer role.

00:02:12.640 --> 00:02:16.820
There have been a lot of very unsubstantial
rumors floating around out there about a return

00:02:16.820 --> 00:02:22.480
to Elm Street, especially with the runaway
success of 2018's Halloween reboot-slash-sequel.

00:02:22.780 --> 00:02:27.160
Now, according to Bloody Disgusting, we can
really expect a new Nightmare on Elm Street

00:02:27.160 --> 00:02:31.860
film to start production in the near future,
but that's about all we know so far.

00:02:31.960 --> 00:02:34.960
"Actually, it's been giving me Freddy nightmares."

00:02:35.580 --> 00:02:39.530
In 2010, there was an attempt to reboot A
Nightmare on Elm Street with Jackie Earle

00:02:39.530 --> 00:02:41.200
Haley playing the lead villain.

00:02:41.200 --> 00:02:45.920
Unfortunately, the reboot was panned by critics
and audiences alike, and the franchise faded

00:02:45.920 --> 00:02:46.840
into the background.

00:02:47.040 --> 00:02:52.440
In September of 2019, Wes Craven's estate
regained the rights to the character and franchise.

00:02:52.640 --> 00:02:56.590
Bloody Disgusting reports that the horror
master's estate is actively seeking pitches

00:02:56.590 --> 00:02:58.140
for the return of Freddy Krueger.

00:02:58.360 --> 00:03:02.900
The site reports that they are accepting pitches
for both a feature film and a possible HBO

00:03:02.900 --> 00:03:03.400
series.

00:03:03.880 --> 00:03:07.940
Obviously, this information is all tied to
the very beginning of the process.

00:03:08.180 --> 00:03:12.140
That said, it seems it won't be too long before
A Nightmare on Elm Street comes back to haunt

00:03:12.140 --> 00:03:12.660
us.

00:03:13.580 --> 00:03:16.960
Interestingly enough, what's thought of as
the classic version of The Fly is, itself,

00:03:16.980 --> 00:03:18.460
a remake.

00:03:18.640 --> 00:03:23.580
Most people think of the 1986 film led by
Jeff Goldblum as the definitive version, but

00:03:23.580 --> 00:03:28.480
the original film actually came out in 1958
and starred horror legend Vincent Price.

00:03:28.840 --> 00:03:33.200
Despite radically different tones and levels
of disturbing imagery, the two start from

00:03:33.200 --> 00:03:38.860
the same basic concept, and both the 1958
film and the 1986 one spawned sequels.

00:03:39.140 --> 00:03:43.560
Considering it's been over 30 years since
Goldblum portrayed Dr. Seth Brundle, of course

00:03:43.560 --> 00:03:45.180
it's about time for a reboot.

00:03:45.300 --> 00:03:49.260
Some were worried that Disney's purchase of
Fox would put the kibosh on more adult fare

00:03:49.260 --> 00:03:51.880
like The Fly, but apparently that isn't the
case.

00:03:52.080 --> 00:03:55.900
According to Movie Hole, The Fly is in no
danger of falling by the wayside.

00:03:56.260 --> 00:03:59.960
It will be interesting to see if they keep
with the teleporter as the culprit, or if

00:03:59.960 --> 00:04:02.000
they switch things up in the third go around.

00:04:02.820 --> 00:04:06.960
Despite the fact that it was essentially riding
on the coattails of Scream, I Know What You

00:04:06.960 --> 00:04:11.150
Did Last Summer actually became a pretty hot
property in the late 1990s.

00:04:11.150 --> 00:04:16.000
The original film was a veritable who's who
of heartthrob actors: Jennifer Love Hewitt,

00:04:16.000 --> 00:04:20.229
Sarah Michelle Gellar, Ryan Phillippe, and
Freddy Prinze Jr. all did battle with "The

00:04:20.229 --> 00:04:22.160
Fisherman" in the campy slasher flick.

00:04:22.300 --> 00:04:26.820
Fans can rejoice: I Know What You Did Last
Summer is returning, this time as an Amazon

00:04:26.820 --> 00:04:27.480
Prime series.

00:04:28.260 --> 00:04:30.340
"What are you waiting for, huh?!"

00:04:30.560 --> 00:04:35.000
James Wan is attached to the series as a producer,
and Bloody Disgusting reports that the series'

00:04:35.000 --> 00:04:36.620
pilot is written by Shay Hatten.

00:04:37.240 --> 00:04:40.200
Hatten also wrote the screenplay for John
Wick 3: Parabellum.

00:04:40.600 --> 00:04:44.180
No director that we know of is attached for
the pilot episode at this point.

00:04:44.189 --> 00:04:48.069
I Know What You Did Last Summer told the story
of a group of teens who run over someone with

00:04:48.069 --> 00:04:50.040
their car and dump the body in the ocean.

00:04:50.320 --> 00:04:54.040
The next year, the group starts receiving
threats from someone who knows their secret,

00:04:54.100 --> 00:04:57.300
and they begin to get killed by a person in
a raincoat carrying a hook.

00:04:58.100 --> 00:05:02.620
Night of the Comet is an oft-forgotten classic,
and a reboot of the low-budget science fiction

00:05:02.620 --> 00:05:04.480
flick could do wonders for the story.

00:05:04.760 --> 00:05:09.139
Roxanne Benjamin, who started out as a producer
on horror films like V/H/S and The Devil's

00:05:09.140 --> 00:05:13.060
Candy before moving into writing and directing,
is attached to the project.

00:05:13.220 --> 00:05:17.200
Night of the Comet finds the earth passing
through the tail of a comet, wiping out almost

00:05:17.200 --> 00:05:18.020
all of humanity.

00:05:18.400 --> 00:05:22.480
Our heroes are two sisters who try to search
for answers while fighting off zombies.

00:05:22.740 --> 00:05:26.460
It's a campy girl power film that has become
a bit of a cult favorite in the years since

00:05:26.460 --> 00:05:28.140
its release in 1984.

00:05:28.400 --> 00:05:31.540
The original film starred Catherine Mary Stewart
and Kelli Maroney.

00:05:31.760 --> 00:05:35.979
Benjamin told Birth.Movies.Death that she
has submitted her screenplay for the reboot,

00:05:35.979 --> 00:05:39.150
and that she hopes the studio will approach
her to direct the movie if they decide to

00:05:39.150 --> 00:05:40.120
go ahead with it.

00:05:40.240 --> 00:05:44.520
Don't expect it anytime soon, however, as
it's, quote, "still very early days."

00:05:45.460 --> 00:05:50.460
Wrong Turn is a surprisingly recent film to
be receiving the remake treatment, but well,

00:05:50.469 --> 00:05:52.490
that's how the business works these days.

00:05:52.490 --> 00:05:57.240
The original film came out in 2003 and spawned
several sequels, with the most recent being

00:05:57.240 --> 00:06:00.160
2014's Wrong Turn 6: Last Resort.

00:06:00.260 --> 00:06:04.780
Strangely, the reboot is being penned by Alan
McElroy, who created the franchise to begin

00:06:04.780 --> 00:06:05.280
with.

00:06:05.400 --> 00:06:09.520
That's good news for fans of the series; if
anyone can get a reboot right, hopefully it's

00:06:09.540 --> 00:06:10.960
the man who created the series.

00:06:11.569 --> 00:06:15.800
The Domestics' Mike P. Nelson is attached
to direct, with a cast led by Emma Dumont,

00:06:15.800 --> 00:06:17.860
Dylan McTee, and Charlotte Vega.

00:06:17.860 --> 00:06:22.129
The original Wrong Turn followed a group of
friends who get lost in rural West Virginia,

00:06:22.129 --> 00:06:25.660
and are terrorized by a cannibalistic family
as they struggle to escape.

00:06:25.900 --> 00:06:26.960
According to Coming Soon:

00:06:27.280 --> 00:06:31.990
"The Wrong Turn reboot will feature a cross-country
hiking expedition that puts a group of friends

00:06:31.990 --> 00:06:36.159
in the land of an inclusive society called
The Foundation, described as people who have

00:06:36.160 --> 00:06:38.420
lived in the mountains since before the Civil
War."

00:06:39.100 --> 00:06:42.400
Another reboot with some strange names attached
to it is Saw.

00:06:42.640 --> 00:06:47.140
The original film was released in 2004, and
quickly became a horror juggernaut.

00:06:47.150 --> 00:06:52.759
Despite a paltry budget of just over one million
dollars, Saw made over $100 million worldwide

00:06:52.760 --> 00:06:54.700
and spawned a massive franchise.

00:06:54.920 --> 00:06:58.900
Director James Wan has gone on to become a
huge star in the industry, and the latest

00:06:58.900 --> 00:07:01.340
sequel came out as recently as 2017.

00:07:01.560 --> 00:07:07.520
And now, Chris Rock; yes, that Chris Rock;
is rebooting the franchise for Lionsgate.

00:07:07.529 --> 00:07:10.719
Rock will feature in the film and serve as
the executive producer.

00:07:10.719 --> 00:07:14.690
Darren Lynn Bousman, who directed the second,
third, and fourth Saw films, is at the helm

00:07:14.690 --> 00:07:15.180
again.

00:07:15.360 --> 00:07:18.820
Max Minghella, Marisol Nichols, and Samuel
L. Jackson star.

00:07:19.160 --> 00:07:23.879
The original Saw series got more and more
insane as the sequels piled up, but it originally

00:07:23.879 --> 00:07:27.949
focused on a serial killer who placed people
in elaborate puzzles to see "how much they

00:07:27.949 --> 00:07:28.940
wanted to live."

00:07:29.960 --> 00:07:31.380
"I want to play a game."

00:07:31.980 --> 00:07:36.240
With Rock and Bousman's reboot, hopefully
some of the magic will return to the franchise.

00:07:37.240 --> 00:07:40.499
Quick quiz: how many Hellraiser movies have
there been?

00:07:40.500 --> 00:07:41.440
Answer: Ten!

00:07:41.540 --> 00:07:42.260
There are ten.

00:07:42.520 --> 00:07:46.200
And the most recent one, Hellraiser: Judgment,
came out in 2018.

00:07:46.210 --> 00:07:51.319
That said, Spyglass Entertainment is trying
to revitalize the franchise a bit with a reboot.

00:07:51.319 --> 00:07:55.749
Yes, the Lament Configuration is headed back
to the big screen, bringing Pinhead and the

00:07:55.749 --> 00:07:57.020
rest of the Cenobites with it.

00:07:57.470 --> 00:08:01.860
The Dark Knight's David S. Goyer is attached
to the reboot as both a writer and producer.

00:08:01.860 --> 00:08:06.199
Clive Barker, who wrote the original story
the series is based on and directed the first

00:08:06.200 --> 00:08:08.820
film in 1987, is also attached.

00:08:09.040 --> 00:08:12.789
Hellraiser never quite reached the level of
massive horror franchises like A Nightmare

00:08:12.789 --> 00:08:17.210
on Elm Street or Halloween, but its dark and
twisted narrative and memorable villain did

00:08:17.210 --> 00:08:19.439
help the series carve out its own fandom.

00:08:19.439 --> 00:08:24.039
The story revolves around a puzzle box that,
when solved, unleashes a gang of demons into

00:08:24.040 --> 00:08:24.720
our world.

00:08:25.040 --> 00:08:28.889
The leader of these demons is Pinhead, one
of the most iconic horror villains of the

00:08:28.889 --> 00:08:29.380
1980s.

00:08:29.880 --> 00:08:32.360
Goyer is excited to be given a chance with
the franchise.

00:08:32.540 --> 00:08:33.600
He told Deadline:

00:08:33.880 --> 00:08:38.860
"Having the chance to reimagine Pinhead and
the Cenobites for a new audience is a nightmare-come-true."

00:08:39.860 --> 00:08:40.360
What's that?

00:08:40.420 --> 00:08:42.160
A successful movie from another country?

00:08:42.720 --> 00:08:47.550
In true American fashion, Train to Busan is
getting a western remake; the buzzworthy zombie

00:08:47.550 --> 00:08:51.120
film out of Korea is in development from James
Wan and Gary Dauberman.

00:08:51.380 --> 00:08:54.880
If you like zombie films, you can't do much
better than Train to Busan.

00:08:55.200 --> 00:09:00.440
The 2016 film follows a group of people stuck
on a moving train as a zombie virus spreads.

00:09:00.800 --> 00:09:05.460
It features some absolutely gruesome scenes
and some very inventive set pieces, and the

00:09:05.460 --> 00:09:08.660
naturally claustrophobic setting is prime
for an outbreak.

00:09:08.790 --> 00:09:12.060
There aren't a lot of details on the remake
at this point in time, but it should be in

00:09:12.060 --> 00:09:17.020
good hands with Wan and Dauberman, two of
the leaders in recent horror success stories.

00:09:17.080 --> 00:09:21.280
Speaking with Entertainment Weekly, Dauberman
explained his approach to the source material:

00:09:21.520 --> 00:09:24.320
"I'm being very careful how we translate it
over here.

00:09:24.320 --> 00:09:26.440
And really my rule is, Don't f-- it up!"

00:09:27.220 --> 00:09:31.880
This one is still extremely early in development,
but we do have a few concrete details on the

00:09:31.880 --> 00:09:33.580
remake of this obscure gem.

00:09:33.680 --> 00:09:38.980
Audrey Rose was released in 1977, a bizarre
little horror mystery starring Marsha Mason

00:09:38.980 --> 00:09:40.160
and Anthony Hopkins.

00:09:40.620 --> 00:09:45.080
Mason plays Janice, a woman with a daughter
whose life is turned upside down when Hopkins'

00:09:45.080 --> 00:09:46.440
Elliot Hoover shows up.

00:09:46.670 --> 00:09:51.420
He insists that Janice's daughter is actually
a reincarnation of his own dead child, and

00:09:51.420 --> 00:09:53.520
all sorts of creepy events start occurring.

00:09:53.760 --> 00:09:57.420
It's a slow burn, but one that could be very
impressive with the right people telling the

00:09:57.420 --> 00:09:58.600
modern adaptation.

00:09:58.700 --> 00:10:02.940
All we know so far about the remake of Audrey
Rose is that it is being released by Orion

00:10:02.959 --> 00:10:06.320
Pictures and the screenplay is being hammered
out by Chloe Okuno.

00:10:06.320 --> 00:10:11.420
Okuno seems like just the writer to put together
a creepy, surreal story like Audrey Rose.

